From b7cdf8cad3d3bef79fa9e2e12597ce4e34c3dad1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 00:10:27 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] HTDESIGNER-111: the code list without the same line twice;
 one click edits an HTML value; the rename selection fix (0.111.0)

- The code list: a listener whose handler is written where it is bound
  (addEventListener('click', function ...)) showed that line twice, as the
  handler and as the binding. Now one row, "binding + handler" (9 on HotPlate's
  Save button).
- The HTML part of the properties: one click on a value is its field, as in the
  property grid (a double-click still works; the id stays not editable).
- Fix: after a rename the selection sometimes went to the form, not the renamed
  one (the real-VS Code rename test flaked on it twice). The rename edits the
  page's scripts too; the page is redrawn for them before the HTML has the new
  name, the probe found nothing and fell back to the form, as 'init' -- and the
  extension took that as the one wanted. The fallback is 'initRoot' now: the
  form shows, the extension keeps asking for the new name, the next drawing
  selects it.

Tests (all 4 layers pass: lib 162, smoke 188, panels, real VS Code 159):
panels (one row per same-line listener, none twice; a click on top = its field,
Esc sends nothing, the id not editable); probe (the one asked for not on the
page: the form, initRoot); smoke (initRoot keeps btnSave, a plain init is taken).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
